JID - 2984699R
PMC - PMC13137745
OAB - What is already known about this topic: (1) Reintegration into civilian life 
      following military separation is a complex and highly individual process 
      influenced by service experiences, personal circumstances, and cultural 
      adjustment. (2) Although research shows that the years immediately after 
      separation are a time of heightened vulnerability, reintegration challenges can 
      persist well beyond the initial transition period. (3) Online assessment 
      platforms reduce stigma, improve accessibility, and enable large-scale data to 
      examine user demand and characteristics. What this topic adds: (1) Demostrates 
      real-world engagement with the M-CARM platform beyond controlled research 
      environments. (2) Confirms scoring consistency with the original validation 
      study. (3) Shows robust psychometric performance under naturalistic conditions, 
      reinforcing the tool's reliability and suitability for applied service contexts.
